        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Honest question, what would be the advantage of porting vim-fugitive instead of using it as is?\r\n\r\nNo one says about porting the whole 'tpope/vim-fugitive'. And no one says the result will have an advantage.\r\n\r\nThe whole idea of 'mini.nivm' is to provide all round out of the box experience with relatively comprehensible code base (with strictly one file per full \"plugin\"). As I consider Git to be an essential part of modern advanced text editor experience, hence 'mini.git' is something I am not against of doing eventually.",
            "created_at": "2023-09-13T18:56:06Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/139#issuecomment-1718155810",
