        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "One thing I love about fugitive is `:Git`: it allows me to leverage all my CLI git-fu (and vice versa, reinforces it) with -- where meaningful -- Vim integration and the convenience of not having to spam a terminal for one-off commands.\r\n\r\nA `mini.git` that offers (only) this interface would be very appealing to me. (You could still create custom mappings for often-used commands, of course.) Benefit would be lower-latency `vim.system` implementation (fugitive can be quite slow if it has to process a lot of content into a buffer).\r\n\r\n(Of course, my pipe dream is https://github.com/libgit2/luagit2 integration in Neovim...)",
            "created_at": "2024-02-25T12:42:20Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/139#issuecomment-1962926444",
            "id": 1962926444,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/issues/139",
